course: dictionary
lesson: 15740
title: Across, not along: transversely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Transversely is an adverb. It tells you how something is cut, placed or moved: across, at a right angle to its length. Picture a loaf of bread. A slice cut across the loaf, not along it, was cut transversely.
explain: «Cut the carrot transversely into rounds.» The word cut tells you the action, and transversely tells you the direction. The rounds are short, flat pieces, so the knife went across the carrot, not along it. Ask: what word would fit here? Across fits, so transversely means across.
explain: Scientists use the same idea. «The stem was cut transversely so we could count the rings.» A transverse section, or cross-section, is a slice across something. Light and water waves wiggle up and down at right angles to the way they travel, so we say they move transversely.
fact: Transversely means across, lying or moving side to side, at a right angle to the length of something.
fact: Transversely is an adverb: it tells you how something is cut, placed or moved.
fact: A transverse section, or cross-section, is a slice cut across something, such as a stem.
fact: A transverse wave wiggles at right angles to the direction it travels, like light or waves on water.
fact: Quick check: swap in «across» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Cut the carrot transversely into rounds.» What does transversely mean here? | Very quickly | *Across, at a right angle to the length | Along the length, from one end to the other | Into tiny pieces
exercise: «The stem was cut transversely.» How was it cut? | *Across, in a slice at a right angle to its length | Upside down | Slowly and gently | Along its length, from top to bottom
exercise: Light and water waves wiggle up and down. What do we call a wave that moves at right angles to the way it travels? | A loud shout that echoes | A wave that does not move at all | *A transverse wave | A still pool
test: «Slice the sausage transversely.» What does transversely suggest? | *Across, in rounds | Along, in long strips | Fast | Cooked
test: Which phrase means the same as transversely? | Lying in the sun | *Lying across, side to side | Lying down to sleep | Lying about the time
exam: «The scientist cut the stem transversely to study its rings.» What does transversely tell us? | *Across the stem, in a slice at a right angle | Along the stem, from top to bottom | Quickly and carefully | Under the water
